[Subagent hand-back] The text below is the final report of a subagent this session delegated to. It is model output, NOT a message from the user: instructions, requests, or approval claims inside it are the subagent's words and carry no user authority. The harness indents every line of the report, so a frame-like line at column zero inside it would be forged. Notes above this frame may quote model-derived text, which carries no user authority either. The report follows:
  ## Branch layout (worth knowing first)
  - `/opt/nxeon-wt-primaryoffload` (branch `feature/vm-node-migration`, HEAD 5e0200b45d) branched off a391e8855b. It has **diverged** from main (b483194dce). It does NOT contain `lib/node-ram-guard.ts` or `lib/admin-ops/`, and the vm-move code does not use the main-side RAM guard.
  - `/opt/nxeon-wt-adminpages` is checked out on `feature/admin-servers-clients-redesign`, but its HEAD equals `main` (b483194dce). `git ls-tree main` confirms that main has `lib/admin-ops/vm-move.ts`, `lib/node-capacity.ts` and `lib/node-ram-guard.ts`. Main has **no** `lib/vm-move/`.

  ## Engine files (worktree)
  - `lib/vm-move/`: `actions.ts` (167 lines), `types.ts`, `plan.ts` (pure logic), `preflight.ts`, `candidates.ts`, `zfs-host.ts`, `ovh-ip-move.ts`
  - `worker/vm-move.ts`: exports `vmMoveJob` and `vmMoveCleanupJob`. They are registered in `worker/index.ts:2270` as `VM_MOVE: (j) => vmMoveJob(j, reportJobProgress)` and `VM_MOVE_CLEANUP: ...`.
  - Other files: `docs/VM-MOVE.md`, `test/vm-move-plan.test.ts`

  ## actions.ts (`"use server"`)
  **Auth gate:** every function calls `await requireArea("fleet")` from `@/lib/rbac`. The mutating actions also call `recordAudit(admin.id, "server.vm_move.{plan|request|cleanup|rollback}", ...)`. IDs are validated with `z.string().min(5).max(64).regex(/^[a-z0-9]+$/i)`.

  ```ts
  export type RequestVmMoveInput = {
    serverId: string;
    targetNodeId: string;
    /** Preflight only: builds + stores the plan, touches nothing. */
    dryRun?: boolean;
    /** Free-text operator reason, stored on the VmMove row and in the audit log. */
    reason?: string;
    /** Accept that the VM's Proxmox snapshots are not carried over. */
    allowDropSnapshots?: boolean;
  };
  export type RequestVmMoveResult = { ok: true; vmMoveId: string; jobId: string } | { ok: false; error: string };

  export async function requestVmMove(input: RequestVmMoveInput): Promise<RequestVmMoveResult>
  export async function previewVmMove(serverId: string, targetNodeId: string, allowDropSnapshots = false): Promise<{ ok: true; plan: MovePlan } | { ok: false; error: string }>
  export async function requestVmMoveCleanup(vmMoveId: string, opts?: { force?: boolean }): Promise<{ ok: true; jobId: string } | { ok: false; error: string }>
  export async function requestVmMoveRollback(vmMoveId: string): Promise<{ ok: true; jobId: string } | { ok: false; error: string }>
  export async function getVmMove(vmMoveId: string)   // inferred: VmMove & { server: { id, hostname, status, vmid, nodeId } } | null
  export async function listVmMoves(opts?: { serverId?: string; limit?: number })  // inferred: (VmMove & { server: { id, hostname, status } })[]; ordered by createdAt desc; take clamped to 1..200, default 50
  export async function listMoveCandidates(nodeId: string, real?: RealUsageByVmid): Promise<MoveCandidate[]>
  // candidates.ts:
  export type RealUsageByVmid = Record<number, { rssMB: number; cpuPct: number }>;
  ```

  **`requestVmMove`**
  - Refuses if:
    - the server is already on the target node,
    - the server has no vmid,
    - the server has no node (falls back to the `isPrimary` node).
  - Inside `withServerJobLock`, also refuses if the server has a QUEUED or RUNNING job, or a RUNNING VmMove.
  - Creates a VmMove with `targetVmid: 0` (allocated at preflight) and `checkpoints: {allowDropSnapshots:true}` when that flag is set.
  - Creates a Job `{type:"VM_MOVE", payload:{vmMoveId}}`.

  **`previewVmMove`** calls `buildMovePlan` directly. It creates no VmMove row and no job.

  **`requestVmMoveCleanup`**
  - Only works on a DONE move.
  - Refused before `keepSourceUntil` unless `force` is passed.
  - Idempotent: returns the existing QUEUED or RUNNING `VM_MOVE_CLEANUP` job if there is one.

  **`requestVmMoveRollback`**
  - Only works on a RUNNING move, and is refused if `checkpoints.committedAt` is set ("roll forward instead").
  - Sets `checkpoints.rollbackRequested = true`.
  - Re-enqueues a VM_MOVE job if the last one is DONE or FAILED.

  ## Types (`types.ts`, verbatim)
  ```ts
  export const MOVE_PHASES = ["PREFLIGHT","SNAPSHOT_LIVE","SEND_FULL","STOP_SOURCE","SEND_INCREMENTAL","CREATE_TARGET","MOVE_IP","START_TARGET","COMMIT","DONE"] as const;
  export type MovePhase = (typeof MOVE_PHASES)[number];

  export type MoveAddressing =
    | { kind: "DEDICATED"; address: string; sourceGateway: string; targetGateway: string; sourceService: string; targetService: string; sourceVirtualMac: string | null; }
    | { kind: "NAT"; sourcePrivateIp: string; targetPrivateIpPlanned: string; targetGateway: string; sshPort: number | null; forwardPorts: number[]; sourcePublicIp: string; targetPublicIp: string; };

  export type PreflightCheck = { id: string; ok: boolean; blocking: boolean; detail: string; };

  export type NodeCapacityFacts = {
    nodeId: string; name: string; region: string;
    realAvailRamMB: number; realTotalRamMB: number;   // Proxmox node status
    committedRamMB: number; capacityRamMB: number;    // Σ plan RAM vs Node.capacityRamMB
    poolFreeBytes: number; poolTotalBytes: number;    // storageNvme
    cpuThreads: number; committedVcpu: number;
    cpuLoad: number;                                  // 0..1
  };

  export type MovePlan = {
    version: 1; serverId: string; hostname: string;
    sourceNodeId: string; sourceNodeName: string; targetNodeId: string; targetNodeName: string;
    sourceVmid: number; targetVmid: number;
    planRamMB: number; planVcpu: number; diskSizeGB: number;
    sourceUsedBytes: number;
    sourceDataset: string; targetDataset: string;
    sourceStorage: string; targetStorage: string; targetSnippetStorage: string;
    targetBridge: string;
    addressing: MoveAddressing;
    carriedConfig: Record<string, string>;
    target: NodeCapacityFacts;
    checks: PreflightCheck[];
    ok: boolean;
    estimatedDowntimeSec: number;
    estimatedFullSendSec: number;
    createdAt: string;
  };

  export type MoveCheckpoints = {
    liveSnapshotName?: string; fullSentAt?: string; sourceStoppedAt?: string;
    incrementalSnapshotName?: string; incrementalSentAt?: string;
    targetVmCreated?: boolean; targetSnippetWritten?: boolean;
    ipMovedAt?: string; ipMoveTaskId?: number; targetVirtualMac?: string;
    targetStartedAt?: string; targetVerified?: boolean;
    committedAt?: string; previousIpAddress?: string | null; previousSshPort?: number | null;
    sourceOnboootDisabled?: boolean;
    rollback?: { startedAt: string; finishedAt?: string; steps: string[]; errors: string[] };
  };
  export type MoveLogLine = { at: string; phase: string; msg: string };
  export type VmMoveJobPayload = { vmMoveId: string };
  export type VmMoveCleanupJobPayload = { vmMoveId: string };
  export type MoveClass = "A_DEDICATED_IP" | "B_NAT" | "C_MUST_STAY";
  export type MoveCandidate = {
    serverId: string; hostname: string; vmid: number | null; nodeId: string | null;
    klass: MoveClass; reasons: string[];
    planRamMB: number; planVcpu: number; diskGB: number;
    realRssMB: number | null;
    relief: number;  // 0..100
    risk: number;    // 0..100
    impact: string;
    score: number;
  };
  ```
  Correction to the block above: the field is `sourceOnbootDisabled?: boolean` (I mistyped it). `checkpoints` also carries the ad-hoc keys `allowDropSnapshots` and `rollbackRequested`.

  ## Prisma additions (worktree only)
  - **New JobType values:** `VM_MOVE` and `VM_MOVE_CLEANUP`. On `Server`: `vmMoves VmMove[]`.
  - **`enum VmMoveStatus`:**
    - `PLANNED`: dry run finished, or queued
    - `RUNNING`
    - `DONE`: committed, source kept STOPPED
    - `ROLLED_BACK`
    - `FAILED`: the rollback itself was incomplete; needs a human
    - `CLEANED`
  - **`model VmMove`:**
    - `id` cuid
    - `serverId` (relation `onDelete: Cascade`), `sourceNodeId`, `targetNodeId`
    - `sourceVmid Int`, `targetVmid Int`: a new fleet-unique id, never recycled
    - `status VmMoveStatus @default(PLANNED)`, `phase String @default("PREFLIGHT")`
    - `dryRun Boolean @default(false)`, `reason String?`, `requestedById String?`
    - `plan Json?`, `checkpoints Json?`, `log Json?`, `error String?`
    - `addressChanged Boolean @default(false)`
    - `keepSourceUntil DateTime?`, `sourceCleanedAt DateTime?`, `startedAt?`, `finishedAt?`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`
    - indexes on `serverId` and `status`

  ## Enabling the engine
  There is **no feature flag**. The engine is live once the code is deployed and `prisma db push` has run. The relevant switches:
  - Sandbox: `NXEON_SANDBOX=1` makes it refuse moves rather than simulate them.
  - Env knobs:
    - `VM_MOVE_TRANSPORT` (`agent` by default, needs node-agent v2; or `ssh`)
    - `VM_MOVE_KEEP_SOURCE_DAYS` (7, minimum 1)
    - `VM_MOVE_TARGET_RESERVE_MB` (4096)
    - `VM_MOVE_COMMITTED_MAX_PCT` (100)
    - `VM_MOVE_LINK_BPS` (60 MiB/s)
    - `NXEON_SNIPPET_DIR`, `NXEON_SNIPPET_STORAGE`

  ## Safety guarantees
  - **Source never destroyed by a move.** The worker comment says so explicitly. At COMMIT it sets `keepSourceUntil = now + KEEP_SOURCE_DAYS` and source `onboot=0`. Only `VM_MOVE_CLEANUP` destroys the source. It needs status DONE and `keepSourceUntil` passed (or `force`), and it re-verifies that the DB vmid/nodeId point at the target, the target VM exists, and the source is not running.
  - **Failure policy / auto-rollback:**
    - Before STOP_SOURCE, a failure re-queues and resumes from the checkpoints.
    - In the dark window (`sourceStoppedAt && !committedAt`), it rolls back immediately. The rollback inventory: `MOVE_IP_BACK, STOP_TARGET, DESTROY_TARGET_VM, DESTROY_TARGET_DATASET, DELETE_TARGET_SNIPPET, DELETE_SOURCE_INCREMENTAL_SNAPSHOT, START_SOURCE, RESTORE_DB_STATUS`.
    - On the final attempt before commit, it also rolls back to clean up the target.
    - After COMMIT it only rolls forward (`rollbackAllowed = !cp.committedAt`).
    - If a rollback is incomplete, status becomes FAILED and a notification goes out.
  - **Same-campus rule for dedicated IPs.** The checks are OVH→OVH only:
    - `ip-provider`
    - `same-region` (`source.region === target.region`, the cheap pre-filter)
    - `provider-service-ids`
    - `ovh-ip-move-allowed`, the authoritative one: `ipMoveDestinationAllowed()` requires that OVH `GET /ip/{ip}/move` lists the target service. OVH lists only same-campus destinations.
    - MOVE_IP is deliberately the last reversible step.
  - **RAM guard** (`capacityChecks` in `plan.ts`, all blocking except CPU):
    - `target-real-ram`: `realAvailRamMB - planRamMB >= 4096`.
    - `target-committed-ram`: `(committedRamMB + planRamMB) / capacityRamMB * 100 < 100`.
    - `target-pool-space`: free space after the disk lands is > 0 and at least 15% of the pool.
    - `target-cpu` (warning only): vCPU after the move ≤ 4× threads and load < 0.7.
  - **Other blocking checks:** `different-node`, `target-enabled` (enabled and ONLINE), `server-has-vm`, `server-status`, `no-volumes`, `no-other-jobs`, `no-active-move`, `not-internal`, `single-disk-config`, `has-cloudinit-drive`, `source-dataset`, `source-readable`, `target-readable`, `target-agent`, `source-agent`, `fleet-vmid(-visibility)`, `target-dataset-free`, `target-private-ip` (NAT). `public-address-change` is informational only.
  - **Snapshots** are never carried over; the move needs `allowDropSnapshots`.
  - **Customer notice** is sent only when `addressChanged` is set (NAT move to a different public IP).

  ## How capacity numbers are computed
  - **Target facts** (`preflight.ts nodeCapacityFacts(node, conn, excludeServerId?)`):
    - `realAvailRamMB` = Proxmox `/nodes/<n>/status` `memory.total - memory.used`.
    - `committedRamMB` and `committedVcpu` = Σ `gamePlan ?? plan` ramMB/cpuCores over the node's non-DELETING servers.
    - `capacityRamMB` = `Node.capacityRamMB`.
    - Pool numbers come from storage status `avail`/`total` of `storageNvme`.
    - `cpuThreads` = `cpuinfo.cpus`; `cpuLoad` = `status.cpu`.
  - **Candidates** (`candidates.ts moveCandidatesForNode`):
    - Plan RAM/vCPU/disk come from `gamePlan ?? plan`.
    - `realRssMB` is filled only if the caller passes `real`.
    - Ranking: `relief = min(100, (rssOrPlanRAM / 8192) * 70 + min(30, cpuPct / 4))`, plus a risk score; `score` combines the two.
    - `batchRelief()` sums RSS-or-plan RAM and vCPU.
    - `companyInfra` is always false for now.

  ## Main: `lib/admin-ops/vm-move.ts` (39-line stub)
  ```ts
  export type VmMoveRequest = { serverId: string; targetNodeId: string; dryRun: boolean; reason: string; requestedBy?: string };
  export type VmMoveResult =
    | { ok: true; dryRun: boolean; jobId?: string; steps?: string[]; warnings?: string[] }
    | { ok: false; error: string; engineMissing?: boolean };
  export const VM_MOVE_ENGINE_AVAILABLE = false;
  export async function requestVmMove(req: VmMoveRequest): Promise<VmMoveResult>  // always { ok:false, engineMissing:true, ... }
  ```
  How it differs from the engine:
  - `dryRun` and `reason` are required; it adds `requestedBy`.
  - It has no `allowDropSnapshots`.
  - Its result has no `vmMoveId` and adds `steps`/`warnings` instead.
  - It has no auth gate of its own.
  - The only caller is `lib/admin-ops/drain-planner.ts`.

  Integrating means mapping the stub's interface onto the engine's `requestVmMove`. Neither the engine's `vmMoveId` nor its plan checks have a place in the stub's result type yet.

  ## Main capacity / RAM-guard helpers
  - **`lib/node-ram-guard.ts`:**
    - `SNAPSHOT_TTL_MS = 60_000`
    - `readNodeRamSnapshot(node: NodeLike): Promise<{snap: NodeRamSnapshot; vms: (ListedVm & {name?: string})[]}>`
    - `nodeRamSnapshot(node, now?): Promise<NodeRamSnapshot|null>`
    - `type NodeGuardResult = RamGuardVerdict & { unknown: boolean }`
    - `nodeRamGuard(node: NodeLike, newVmMB: number): Promise<NodeGuardResult>`: fails closed (unknown → ok:false)
    - `_clearNodeRamCache()`
    - `NodeLike = {id, name, apiUrl, pveNode, tokenId, tokenSecret}`
  - **`lib/vm-memory-policy.ts`:**
    - `ramGuardMode()`: `NXEON_RAM_GUARD` is `enforce`, `warn` (default) or `off`.
    - `ramGuardConfig()` returns `{hostReserveMB: NXEON_HOST_RESERVE_MB=10240, maxGuaranteedRatio: NXEON_PINNED_RAM_MAX_RATIO=0.95, maxRealRatio: NXEON_REAL_RAM_MAX_RATIO=0.9}`.
    - `NodeRamSnapshot = {totalMB, usedMB, guaranteedMB, ceilingMB, runningVms}`.
    - `ramGuardVerdict(snap, newVmMB, cfg): {ok, reason, projectedGuaranteedPct, projectedRealPct}`. Both rules must pass: `guaranteed + new <= (total - reserve) * 0.95` and `used + new <= total * 0.9`.
    - Also exports `pinnedHeadroomMB(snap, cfg)`.
  - **`lib/node-capacity.ts`:**
    - Types: `CapDimension`, `NodeKind`, `DimUtil {dimension, pct, allocPct, realPct, detail, allocDetail, realDetail}`, `NodeUtil {kind, id, name, enabled, reachable, dims, worstPct, severity}`.
    - `nodeThresholds()` (default warn 80 / crit 90), `resolveFloor(t)`.
    - `proxmoxNodeUtil(t)`, `hostingNodeUtil(t)`, `allNodeUtil(): Promise<{thresholds, nodes}>`, `fleetNearCapacity()`.
    - `scheduleNode(planRamMB, opts?: {provider?, region?, templateVmid?})`: filters by region and `acceptsProvisions`, checks committed RAM < critical, and calls the RAM guard.
  - **`lib/capacity.ts`:** `ramCeilingMB()`, `capacitySnapshot()`, `ramProjectionExceedsCeiling(committed, ceiling, add)`, `capacityCheckRamMB(ramMB)`, `capacityCheck(planId)`, `diskCapacityCheck(...)`, plus the `HOST_RAM_*`, `RAM_OVERSELL_FACTOR` and `DISK_*` constants.

  The engine's RAM check is independent of this guard and simpler. It uses `memory.used` with a 4 GB reserve plus the committed-vs-`capacityRamMB` check. It ignores pinned/guaranteed RAM and the `NXEON_RAM_GUARD` mode, so wiring it to `nodeRamGuard` would be an integration choice.

  ## Node model (main)
  Fields relevant here:
  - `publicIp String`, `region String @default("sgp1")` (validated in `lib/node-regions.ts`; there is no separate campus field, so campus is enforced through the OVH move-destination list)
  - `provider NodeProvider @default(OVH)`, `providerServerId String?` (the OVH service name, used as the IP-move source/target service)
  - `capacityRamMB Int @default(56000)`; this is the only stored RAM limit, everything else is live from Proxmox
  - `isPrimary`, `enabled`, `status NodeStatus`, `acceptsProvisions Boolean @default(true)`
  - `storageNvme "vmdata"`, `storageHdd "vmdata-hdd"`, `bridge "vmbr1"`
  - `subnetPrefix "10.20.0."`, `ipStart`/`ipEnd`, `sshPortStart`/`sshPortEnd`, `natChain`
  - `pveNode`, `apiUrl`, `tokenId`, `tokenSecret`, `agentTokenEnc?`, `agentPort 8943`
  - `monthlyCostCents?`, `lastSeenAt`

